# .goosehints

## Commits

The user commits manually. Never create commits. Instead, provide the
commit text (message + body) once changes are complete and reviewed.

## Commands (just)

```bash
just check               # full workspace build check
just test                # all unit tests (types + app)
just test-types          # kid-types tests (task model, storage)
just test-app            # kid-app tests (scheduling, upcoming)
just test-one <name>     # single test by name
just test-e2e            # browser e2e (needs running server)
```

## Code Style

Always implement the `Deref` trait for single-field newtype wrappers to
avoid `.0` field access.

## Web UI Design

ADHD-friendly UX is a hard requirement. Prioritize:
- Add salience, don't subtract it (highlight important items
  rather than dimming less important ones)
- Minimal visual channels per distinction (one signal, not three)
- Equal readability everywhere — hierarchy through accent, not deficit
- Reduce cognitive load: fewer competing visual patterns, consistent
  sizing, no unnecessary animation
